from pathlib import Path
p=Path('navigation-language-final-audit');s='''<!doctype html><html lang="en"><meta charset="utf-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1"><title>DommyDom navigation and language menu review</title><style>body{margin:0;background:#f4f1eb;color:#343c32;font:16px/1.6 Arial,sans-serif}main{max-width:1700px;margin:auto;padding:28px}h1,h2{font-weight:400}.pair{display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr;gap:18px;margin-bottom:32px}figure{margin:0;padding:12px;background:white}img{display:block;width:100%;height:auto}a{color:#48533e}.status{background:white;border-left:3px solid #68705e;padding:18px 22px;margin:24px 0}@media(max-width:700px){.pair{grid-template-columns:1fr}}</style><main><h1>Navigation and language menu: actual before and after</h1><p>Sidebar redesigned with a branded editorial masthead, a distinct property-and-design zone, clear category hierarchy, selective grouping and inline submenus. The existing 200px content reservation, every destination, photographs and page copy are retained. Language choices use a compact two-column matrix with consistent left alignment. No long legal copy is inside the selection list; the small Notice control opens the separate legal notice.</p><div class="status"><strong>Translation is not live.</strong> The endpoint configuration is empty. No Google project or application credentials are configured in this workspace, and no backend deployment or billing approval has been provided. An approved billing-enabled project, Cloud Translation API, runtime service identity/permissions, Firestore cache and quota records, rate-limit secret, and deployed HTTPS endpoint are still required. Local tests exercised persistence, same-page state, English restoration, RTL and input exclusions with an explicitly labeled echo transport. That is not Google translation. No simulated translated screenshots are presented. <a href="../translation-service/SETUP.md">Exact setup steps and permissions</a>.</div>'''
for w in [768,820,834,1024,1180,1440,390]:
 s+=f'<h2>{w}px</h2>'
 for kind in (['closed','expanded','language'] if 600<=w<1200 else ['closed','language']):
  s+=f'<p>{kind.title()}</p><div class="pair">'
  for phase in ['before','after']:
   f=f'{phase}-{w}-{kind}.png';f='final/'+f if phase=='after' else f;s+=f'<figure><figcaption>{phase.title()}</figcaption><a href="{f}"><img src="{f}" alt="{phase} {kind} at {w} pixels" loading="lazy"></a></figure>'
  s+='</div>'
s+='''<p>Shared assets verified in the actual browser: tablet-language.css?v=20261015-navigation-language-v2 and google-translation.js?v=20261015-compact. Desktop language hover, tablet/phone tap, left-aligned RTL labels, a selection panel under 350px tall, and the separate legal notice were checked. All five requested tablet widths were visually inspected closed and expanded. Nothing committed, pushed, published or billed.</p><p>Attribution retained according to <a href="https://docs.cloud.google.com/translate/attribution">Google attribution requirements</a>.</p></main></html>''';(p/'review.html').write_text(s,encoding='utf-8')
